,{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-5","number":"2B","markdown":"Using Taylor series method, find an approximate value of $y$ when $x=0.1$ given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=x-y^2;\\quad y(0)=1,\n$$\n\ncarryout upto fourth order derivative terms in the series, correct to 4 decimal places.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-5-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1201,1445,166]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-6","number":"2C","markdown":"Using Simpson’s $\\tfrac{1}{3}^{\\mathrm{rd}}$ rule to find an approximate value for the integral\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{0.6} e^{-x^2}\\,dx\n$$\n\nby taking 6 subintervals and correct to 4 decimal places.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-6-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1359,1445,159]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-7","number":"3A","markdown":"Using Gram-Schmidt orthonormalization process find an orthonormal basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ from the set of vectors $\\{(1,-1,1),(1,0,1),(1,1,2)\\}$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-7-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1510,1445,142]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-8","number":"3B","markdown":"Solve $(2xy-\\sin x)\\,dx+(x^2-\\cos y)\\,dy=0$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-8-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1644,1445,124]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-9","number":"3C","markdown":"Solve\n\n$$\n\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}+3\\frac{dy}{dx}+2y=x^2+3x+1.\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-9-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,78,1445,150]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-10","number":"4A","markdown":"Show that the vectors $S=\\{(1,1,1),(1,2,3),(2,-1,1)\\}$ form a basis for $\\mathbb{R}^3$. Express the vector $(2,5,4)$ in terms of basis vectors.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-10-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,220,1445,133]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-11","number":"4B","markdown":"Using method of variation of parameters, evaluate\n\n$$\n\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}-2\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=e^x\\log x.\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-11-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,345,1445,157]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-12","number":"4C","markdown":"Using Gauss elimination method, solve the system equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx+y+z&=6\\\\\nx-y+2z&=5\\\\\n3x+y+z&=8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-12-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,494,1445,251]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-13","number":"5A","markdown":"Using power method, obtain the numerically largest eigen value and corresponding eigen vector of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3&4&-2\\\\1&4&-1\\\\2&6&-1\\end{bmatrix}$ correct to 2 decimals, after 4 iterations. Take initial approximate eigen vector as $X^{(0)}=\\begin{bmatrix}0\\\\1\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-13-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,737,1445,318]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-14","number":"5B","markdown":"Solve\n\n$$\nx^2\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}-3x\\frac{dy}{dx}+5y=x^2\\sin(\\ln x).\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-14-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,1046,1445,134]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"d7c37ffbfc4856500267-q-15","number":"5C","markdown":"Using Gauss Seidel method solve the following system of equations,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10x+2y+z&=9\\\\\n-2x+3y+10z&=22\\\\\nx+10y-z&=-22\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPerform 3 iterations and correct the solution up to 4 decimals by taking the initial approximation as $x=y=z=0$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/d7c37ffbfc4856500267/q-15-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,1172,1445,596]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]}],"warnings":["Transcribed from original page images with gpt-5.4-mini. Automatic transcription is not independent human verification."]}
